  "is_sufficient": false,
  "knowledge_gaps": [
    "Frequency-bin matching does not isolate lexical similarity: within-bin popularity, text availability and duplicate product variants can still differ. Report balance diagnostics and describe the result as a conditional candidate-set comparison.",
    "Control-pool overlap is unspecified. Allowing lexical items in controls can dilute the comparison; excluding them can make matching infeasible and change the estimand. Predeclare this choice and report overlap and matching coverage.",
    "Reproduction requires fixed frequency-bin boundaries, TF-IDF settings, prefix-text aggregation, user/prefix selection, history truncation, repeated-draw counts, bootstrap configuration and handling of repeated targets already present in histories.",
    "The pseudocode should index B × L × D features by batch and final nonpadding position, add definitions for every new metric, and avoid restarting seed 42 for each control draw.",
    "Training memorization and metadata shortcuts limit generalization. The potential rating of 7 lacks validation evidence; implementation difficulty 4 is plausible only if the existing retrieval and audit infrastructure is reusable. Diagnostic runtime also needs an explicit budget.",
    "The NextItNet reference title is inaccurate and should be checked against arXiv:1808.05163. No supplied evidence establishes that this diagnostic should take priority over a controlled single-model training-sampler experiment."
  ],
  "follow_up_queries": [
    {
      "reason": "Clarify matching assumptions, residual imbalance and control overlap before interpreting lexical difficulty.",
      "query": "In recommender-system hard-negative evaluation, how should popularity-matched lexical candidate sets and random controls be constructed? Find methods addressing coarse frequency-bin residual imbalance, overlapping candidate sets, common support, missing metadata and balance diagnostics."
    },
    {
      "reason": "Determine whether the proposed training-only audit can inform a useful next experiment without confusing memorization or false negatives with preference quality.",
      "query": "Sequential recommendation hard-negative sampling lexical similarity popularity matching false negatives training memorization: what controlled studies connect frozen training candidate-difficulty diagnostics to held-out ranking improvements, and what single-model sampler ablations are recommended?"
    },
    {
      "reason": "Complete the statistical protocol and verify that calibration claims remain limited to the specified candidate pool.",
      "query": "For recommendation evaluation with 99 unique uniformly sampled negatives, how are hypergeometric hit@10 calibration, deterministic score ties, repeated candidate draws and paired user-cluster bootstrap intervals implemented? Explain uncertainty conditional on one fitted model and a bounded exact-catalog subset."
    }
  ]
}
